    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d730">

                <pb facs="1018" n="1008" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg1008"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/9–2146: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-09-21T13:00:00+09:00">September 21,
                            1946—1 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received September 25—1:42 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1518. General Marshall has approved for transmission following message from him
                    to Acting Secretary of State (1538): <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Reference your 518<anchor n="50" xml:id="d730-f1"/> and my 1235<anchor
                                n="51" xml:id="d730-f2"/> of July, I would not object to ‘working
                            level’ discussion regarding material or technical assistance for the
                            reconstruction or repair of rail communications because they are
                            urgently needed as the basis for reconstituting a reasonable national
                            economy. Otherwise, I concur in Department’s views outlined in Urtel
                            758, September 16, 8 p.m.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
